# Everything the extension needs at runtime is bundled into out/ by build.mjs,
# so the VSIX ships no node_modules at all. Previously the whole dependency tree
# was packaged, which meant shipping ~21 MB of js-tiktoken.
#
# Deny everything, then allow back only what the extension and the marketplace
# listing need.
#
# The allow-list is deliberately narrow: `!out/**` followed by an `out/**/*.map`
# exclusion does NOT work — vsce applies negations last, so the broad negation
# wins and source maps from a development build end up in the VSIX along with
# the full TypeScript source. Allow only the files we actually ship.
**

!out/*.js
!out/encodings/*.js
!package.json
!README.md
!CHANGELOG.md
!LICENSE
!THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES.md
!icon.png
